  "summary": "Recent preprints model cell, donor and clone states in single-cell, long-read and buccal methylation data using structured, interpretable representations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned decomposition of heterogeneity into interpretable components at the level of cells, donors or clones. scPACE uses a hierarchical personalized variational autoencoder to learn separate cell and donor states in cohort single-cell transcriptomics and to impute missing cells. LongReadClock assigns long-read whole-genome reads from bulk blood to cell types by methylation-based likelihood scoring, yielding cell-type-resolved epigenetic aging clocks. CheekAI pairs a deep learning epigenetic aging clock trained on buccal methylation data with explainability over lifestyle and health biomarker proxies. ChronoClone groups single-cell clones into metaclones by time-resolved cell-state composition and links clonal behaviour to lineage output. What is new is the attribution of aging and clonal variation to specific cell types, donors or clones. The items do not share a single focus on technical correction.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
